```typescript
export type SwatchDraft = { name: string; colors: string[] };
export type StoredDraft = SwatchDraft & { id: number };

export class DraftShelf {
  add(draft: SwatchDraft): StoredDraft;
  getAll(): StoredDraft[];
  remove(id: number): boolean;
}
```

A name must be a non-empty string after trimming and is stored trimmed. `colors` must be a non-empty array of strings matching exactly `#[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}`; preserve spelling and order. Malformed drafts throw `TypeError`. IDs start at 1, increase monotonically, and are never reused. `getAll` returns insertion order. `remove` throws `RangeError` unless `id` is a positive integer and returns `false` when a valid ID is absent. Inputs and all outputs must be defensively copied, including color arrays. Failed operations must not mutate state or consume an ID.

